      "refersTo": "category-tab",
      "description": "Ruled category control with graphite selection and an orange arrow.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-category-rail\" role=\"tablist\" aria-label=\"Fleet categories\"><button class=\"ds-category-tab ds-category-selected\" role=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Foundation <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M7 7h10v10M7 17 17 7\"/></svg></button><button class=\"ds-category-tab\" role=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"false\">Lifting <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M7 7h10v10M7 17 17 7\"/></svg></button></div>",
      "css": ".ds-category-rail{border-top:1px solid #bdc1b3;max-width:320px;}.ds-category-tab{font-family:var(--display,Barlow,'Arial Narrow',sans-serif);width:100%;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;font-size:26px;line-height:1.65;padding:21px 17px;border:0;border-bottom:1px solid #bdc1b3;background:none;color:var(--ink,#171917);text-align:left;cursor:pointer;transition:background .3s,color .3s;}.ds-category-selected{background:var(--ink,#171917);color:var(--paper,#f4f3ec);border-color:var(--ink,#171917);}.ds-category-selected svg{color:var(--orange,#ff6b2c);}.ds-category-tab:hover:not(.ds-category-selected){background:#dde0d4;}.ds-category-tab:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--focus,#cb4d15);outline-offset:5px;}@media(max-width:900px){.ds-category-rail{display:flex;max-width:none;overflow-x:auto;}.ds-category-tab{font-family:var(--body,DM,Arial,sans-serif);flex-shrink:0;width:auto;padding:16px 20px;border:0;gap:20px;font-size:11px;}}@media(max-width:640px){.ds-category-tab{font-size:12px;padding:15px;gap:15px;}}@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.ds-category-tab{transition:none;}}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Cinematic industrial",
    "overview": "Heavy machinery supplies the scale, material and atmosphere. Warm ivory reading surfaces, graphite foundations and a clear orange accent carry an ambitious industrial identity without making equipment selection feel complicated. Photography earns the dramatic moments; condensed type provides confidence and compact emphasis.\n\nEditorial sections are spacious, while catalogues, specifications, documents and forms are quieter and more closely ruled. Controls remain practical and flat. The same pairing of photographic authority and warm-paper clarity carries across public pages and the local enquiry workspace. Illustrative concept imagery is identified honestly rather than presented as evidence of a specific project.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Monumental machinery photography and tightly set condensed headings.",
      "Warm ivory and graphite surfaces with purposeful orange actions.",
      "Flat equipment grids, ruled specifications and square editorial geometry.",
      "Restrained image motion, explicit selected states and visible keyboard focus.",
      "Mobile equipment labels remain readable at their observed 12px size."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Orange Points the Way Rule",
        "body": "Orange marks actions and meaningful emphasis. Keep long reading passages in graphite or the established secondary neutrals.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Compressed Display, Open Task Rule",
        "body": "Reserve condensed type for headings and equipment names. Use DM Sans for actions, specifications, forms and navigation.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Shared Edge Rule",
        "body": "Align text, photographic panels, rules and grids to the responsive container edges. Use internal padding only where a surface genuinely contains a component.",
        "section": "layout"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat at Rest Rule",
        "body": "Keep editorial panels, catalogue cards and forms unshadowed. Reserve the observed shadows for navigation overlays and transient feedback.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Square Field Rule",
        "body": "Keep content fields and photographic compositions square. Apply small corners to controls and circles to the observed arrow/status devices.",
        "section": "shapes"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** pair warm-paper reading surfaces with graphite photographic and support surfaces.",
      "**Do** use orange for a meaningful action or clear emphasis, and graphite or established neutrals for reading copy.",
      "**Do** use the locally hosted condensed display faces and DM Sans body faces through their existing aliases.",
      "**Do** keep equipment grids and specification rows flat, square and aligned to shared container edges.",
      "**Do** preserve visible keyboard focus, explicit selected states and the reduced-motion behavior.",
      "**Do** keep mobile fleet labels at their observed 12px size and disclose illustrative machinery imagery where the source does."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** replace the restrained industrial palette with unrelated decorative accents.",
      "**Don't** turn equipment cards or forms into rounded, shadowed or glass panels.",
      "**Don't** set task copy, navigation or input content in the condensed display face.",
      "**Don't** replace photographic image scrims with illegible unprotected overlay text.",
      "**Don't** generalize the observed 108px display exceptions, tiny ancillary captions or decorative vertical slogan into reusable rules.",
      "**Don't** imply verified project evidence, exact model photography, price or availability through an illustrative visual."
    ]
  }
}
